  "tensions": [
    "PKD claims the dialectic is within God alone, not God vs. Satan, yet he also speaks of two 'Gods' in VALIS—the dramatic device risks obscuring the theological unity he asserts",
    "Logos always wins, yet the dark side has 'all the power or virtually all the power'—how does reason overcome power? (PKD answers: through a priori knowledge, but this remains conceptually unsettling)",
    "PKD identifies Ansel Archer as Logos but notes she denies the Valis experience that created her—is Logos inherently self-denying or contradictory?",
    "The experience was both internal vision and external perception (macro-form of inner vision)—PKD resolves this by saying both are the same dialectic, but the collapse of inner-outer remains philosophically unclear",
    "PKD saw Valis 'without verbal ratiocination' but later interprets it through Hegel, Boehme, process theology—the gap between pre-rational revelation and rational reconstruction haunts the text",
